---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About — HueForge"
	description="HueForge is a single-purpose, free browser-based color palette generator. Learn why it exists, how it works, and why your colors never leave your device."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About HueForge</h1>

		<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#5C4F3D]">
			<p>
				HueForge does one thing: it turns a single color into a complete,
				usable palette, entirely inside your browser. There's no account
				to create, no upload to wait on, and no server that ever sees the
				color you pick.
			</p>
			<p>
				We built it as a single-purpose tool on purpose. Rather than
				bundling a dozen unrelated utilities behind one confusing homepage,
				HueForge is exactly, only, a color palette generator &mdash; so it
				loads fast, stays focused, and does the one job well.
			</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#2B2013]">
				How it works
			</h2>
			<p>
				When you type a hex code or use the native color picker, HueForge
				converts that color to HSL (hue, saturation, lightness) and rotates
				the hue around the color wheel to derive three classic palette
				types: a complementary color 180&deg; away for maximum contrast,
				two analogous colors 30&deg; to either side for a harmonious feel,
				and two triadic colors 120&deg; apart for a balanced three-color
				scheme. Every hex, RGB, and HSL value shown is computed with plain
				JavaScript color math &mdash; there is no server round-trip and no
				external color API involved.
			</p>
			<p>
				Because everything happens on your device, nothing you pick is
				ever transmitted, logged, or stored anywhere. Close the tab and
				it's gone, exactly as if you'd never opened it.
			</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#2B2013]">
				Why it's free
			</h2>
			<p>
				HueForge is supported by small, unobtrusive advertising rather than
				subscriptions or paywalls. There's nothing to sign up for and no
				limit on how many palettes you generate.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
